# AI Stack 2026 — image pins.  COMMITTED, Renovate-managed (final-design §7.1).
#
# Every reference in compose is ${X_TAG:?pin missing}@${X_DIGEST:?pin missing},
# so a missing pin fails closed instead of silently resolving to :latest.
#
# Per image this file carries: the tag, the registry digest, whether the version
# is a LATEST PUBLISHED RELEASE or a LATEST TAG, and the date the digest was
# checked.  `aistack install|update|pin` renders this into a delimited block in
# the generated .env; CI (I4) asserts the rendered block matches this file, and
# `aistack doctor` re-checks — which is what catches a Renovate PR merged
# without a re-render.
#
# SUPPLY-CHAIN POSTURE, STATED HONESTLY (final-design §7.1):
#   DIGEST PINNING IS THE CONTROL.  `cosign verify` runs opportunistically, only
#   for the upstreams that publish signatures, listed per image below.  There is
#   no blanket "images are verified" claim and this file will not make one.
#
# Digests below were resolved on 2026-10-18 from the live registries with
# `docker buildx imagetools inspect` on AI-Sandbox.  Each is the MULTI-ARCH
# INDEX digest, which is what `docker pull <ref>@<digest>` takes.
#
# VERIFIED: the tag->digest mapping (measured).
# [A]:      cosign signature availability per upstream — NOM-258 has not probed
#           each upstream's signing posture; the column below says "unprobed"
#           rather than "unsigned", because those are different claims.

# --- core (8) ---------------------------------------------------------------

