# PostgreSQL 17 + pgvector 0.8.7.  One datastore, one backup procedure, a
# database and a NON-SUPERUSER ROLE PER APP.
#
# THE -trixie VARIANT (Debian 13), NOT the default bookworm one.  This was
# V7's `measured_alternative` and it is now APPLIED: the Tech Lead decided
# yes on NOM-341.  It trades CRITICAL units 8 -> 2 for HIGH 20 -> 28,
# measured at this exact digest in security-report-bump-20261019T060718Z.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL CONDITION THAT CAME WITH THE DECISION (V7 `recommendation`):
# Debian 13 carries a glibc collation change.  Taking this on a FRESH install
# is a non-issue and the MVP installs fresh.  Taking it as an in-place base
# swap under an EXISTING PGDATA requires a REINDEX.
#
# THAT CONDITION IS NOW BOTH ENFORCED AND PERFORMED (NOM-354, 2026-10-23).
# It used to end "and nothing in this repo performs one", which was true for
# two months and was enforced by nothing: `aistack update` renders this pin
# and recreates the container, so a plain update would have done exactly what
# the sentence forbade.
#   * scripts/preflight-collation.sh refuses the swap, and update.sh runs it
#     as step 2 -- before the backup, the render, the pull and the recreate.
#   * scripts/migrate-collation.sh performs the migration, idempotently.
#   * tests/collation-migration.sh covers both, in tests/run.sh's stack tier.
#
# AND THE CHANGE IS BIGGER THAN THIS COMMENT SAID.  The base swap moved TWO
# collation providers, not one: glibc 2.36 -> 2.41 AND ICU 153.120 -> 153.128.
# ALTER DATABASE ... REFRESH COLLATION VERSION covers the database default
# only, so after doing just that, this cluster still held 5663 stale
# pg_collation rows -- 2 libc and 807 ICU per database -- and postgres warns
# whenever such a collation is used.  A "glibc collation change" is the
# trigger, not the whole job.
#
# The sandbox cluster was moved onto this pin on 2026-10-23: all 7 databases
# reindexed, both catalogs re-recorded at 2.41/153.128, 0 warnings, doctor
# clean.  Measured there: en_US.utf8 ORDERING did not move between 2.36 and
# 2.41 over 6000 mixed latin/accented/Arabic strings, so this is a
# correctness gate rather than observed corruption -- which is one locale and
# one sample, not a proof that any locale is safe.  The reindex stays
# mandatory.
POSTGRES_IMAGE=docker.io/pgvector/pgvector
POSTGRES_TAG=0.8.7-pg17-trixie
POSTGRES_DIGEST=sha256:7a7e9f22015b67edb4bef5c59daeebcd7e74bfa570df6ce60ae01237c8648a84
POSTGRES_KIND=latest-published-release
POSTGRES_CHECKED=2026-10-20
POSTGRES_COSIGN=unprobed

